# ${project_name}

A small Go command-line project that uses only the standard library.

## Run

Requires Go 1.22 or newer. Run the commands from this directory.

```sh
go run .
```

## Test and build

```sh
go test ./...
go vet ./...
go build -o bin/${binary_name} .
```

## Extend the project

Keep `main` limited to process setup and exit handling. `run(io.Writer)` contains
the command behavior and can be tested with an in-memory buffer or a failing
writer. Add reusable logic alongside `calculator.go`; introduce subpackages when
there is a real boundary, not just to populate directories.

The sample `add` follows Go's native integer arithmetic; it is not a checked
financial or arbitrary-precision calculator. Run `gofmt -w .` after edits.
